---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---
<DocsLayout title="CLI Reference" activeSlug="cli-reference" description="Reference for every pas-agent command and flag: init, update, remove, checkpoint, status, list, and export.">
  <h1>CLI Reference</h1>

  <p>
    PAS-Agent is a single binary, <code>pas-agent</code>. Every command except
    <code>init</code> finds the session by walking up from the current directory.
  </p>

  <h2>pas-agent init</h2>
  <p>Create a new session.</p>
  <pre><code>pas-agent init [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -n, --name &lt;NAME&gt;   Project name (defaults to the project directory name)
  -t, --task &lt;TASK&gt;   Task description (prompted for if omitted)</code></pre>
  <p>
    Creates <code>.pas-agent/session.json</code> at the git repository root, or in the
    current directory outside git, and records the current git state.
  </p>

  <h2>pas-agent update</h2>
  <p>Change the task state. List flags can be repeated; each value is one item.</p>
  <pre><code>pas-agent update [OPTIONS]

Options:
  --task &lt;TASK&gt;          Set task description
  --objective &lt;OBJ&gt;      Set objective
  --next &lt;ACTION&gt;        Set next action
  --clear-next           Clear the next action
  --completed &lt;ITEM&gt;     Add a completed item
  --remaining &lt;ITEM&gt;     Add a remaining item
  --decision &lt;ITEM&gt;      Add a decision
  --blocker &lt;ITEM&gt;       Add a blocker
  --constraint &lt;ITEM&gt;    Add a constraint
  --discovery &lt;ITEM&gt;     Add a discovery
  --done &lt;N&gt;             Move remaining item #N to completed
  --resolve &lt;N&gt;          Remove resolved blocker #N</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>N</code> is the number shown by <code>pas-agent status</code>. Numbered operations
    run before items are added, so the numbers match what you saw. If any number is
    invalid, nothing is changed.
  </p>

  <h2>pas-agent remove</h2>
  <p>Remove items from a list by number.</p>
  <pre><code>pas-agent remove &lt;LIST&gt; &lt;N&gt;...

Lists: completed, remaining, decisions, blockers, constraints, discoveries</code></pre>

  <h2>pas-agent checkpoint</h2>
  <p>Save a checkpoint of the current session state.</p>
  <pre><code>pas-agent checkpoint [MESSAGE...]</code></pre>
  <p>
    Records the git state, the files with uncommitted changes, and a snapshot of the
    task state. You're prompted for a message if you don't give one.
  </p>

  <h2>pas-agent status</h2>
  <p>
    Show the session: task, numbered lists, live git state, and the latest checkpoint.
  </p>
  <pre><code>pas-agent status</code></pre>

  <h2>pas-agent list</h2>
  <p>List all checkpoints with timestamp, message, file count, and commit.</p>
  <pre><code>pas-agent list</code></pre>

  <h2>pas-agent export</h2>
  <p>Write session context into the file a target agent reads at startup.</p>
  <pre><code>pas-agent export --to &lt;AGENT&gt; [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -t, --to &lt;AGENT&gt;      claude-code, codex, opencode, kiro-cli, antigravity, gemini-cli, cursor
  -o, --output &lt;PATH&gt;   Output file (defaults to CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md or GEMINI.md in the project root)
      --force           Replace the whole file instead of only the PAS-Agent block</code></pre>
  <p>
    Unknown targets are rejected. See <a href="/docs/portable-state">Portable State</a>
    for how the block is written.
  </p>

  <h2>Examples</h2>
  <pre><code># Initialize with task
pas-agent init --task "Implement user authentication"

# Record progress
pas-agent update --completed "Login endpoint" --completed "Password hashing" \
                 --remaining "Token refresh" --next "Implement token refresh"

# Finish remaining item #1
pas-agent update --done 1

# Save checkpoint
pas-agent checkpoint "Login complete"

# Export for Codex
pas-agent export --to codex</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
